12. Expected Outcome
Significant reduction in automated spam enquiries.
Improved user experience for domestic and NRI customers.
Industry-standard security aligned with modern web practices.
Reduced administrative overhead from spam email handling.
Enhanced trust and professionalism for Propertism's public-facing forms.
Implementation Recommendation

This SCCB should be implemented as a reusable Spam Protection Framework rather than a one-off contact form enhancement. The verification component should be encapsulated as a shared module so that every current and future public-facing form (Contact, Property Enquiry, Site Visit, Callback, Sell/Rent Property, Newsletter, etc.) can adopt the same protection with minimal additional development. This ensures consistent security, easier maintenance, and centralized configuration across the Propertism platform.